# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host state out of the image.
#
# node_modules and wwwroot matter most: both are build output. If a stale wwwroot from a
# local build were copied in, it would be overwritten by the client stage — but node_modules
# built on Windows would break the Linux install outright.

.git
.github
.vs
.idea

**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

# Local build output; the image builds its own.
src/Split.Api/wwwroot

# Local databases. Never ship one: it would overwrite the mounted disk's path at build time
# and bake somebody's test data into a public image.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

docs
README.md
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
